# AI Coach verification (Cursor only — not for the public app)

When the user asks to verify chatbot answers, run QA, or says questions should appear "here not on the website":

1. **Do not** add benchmark questions, answer keys, CSV export buttons, or coach-review prompts to the React UI unless they explicitly ask for a website feature.
2. Reference dev-only files in the project root: `chat_questions_log.csv`, `clients_data.csv`, and `node export_clients.js` — these are for you in Cursor, not for the live site.
3. In **this Cursor chat**, present each question below, give a correct coaching answer, then compare to `generateAIResponse` in `AIChatbot.jsx` and note gaps.

## Standard verification questions

| # | Question | What a correct answer must cover |
|---|----------|----------------------------------|
| 1 | What should I eat 1 hour before heavy squatting? | Small, easy-to-digest meal/snack; carbs + moderate protein; low fat/fiber; hydration; timing ~1–2 h before heavy work (1 h is tight — lighter snack OK). |
| 2 | Is it okay to train if my legs are still sore? | DOMS vs sharp pain; mild soreness + reduced volume/intensity OK; skip or modify if pain alters form; sleep/hydration/active recovery. |
| 3 | How many sets per muscle group should I do for hypertrophy? | ~10–20 hard sets/muscle/week (evidence range); 8–12 reps common; RPE 7–9; progression; rest days. |
| 4 | What should I eat before training? | Same as #1 — balanced carbs + protein, timing, avoid heavy fats right before session. |
| 5 | How many sets for muscle growth? | Same as #3. |
| 6 | Warm-up / stretch before lifting? | Dynamic warm-up 5–10 min; avoid long static stretching pre-heavy lifts; CNS prep. |

After answering in chat, suggest minimal code changes only if the in-app bot reply is misleading or off-topic for the question asked.
